{"title":"Popliteal vein is superficial to the artery","preview":"The vein-artery relationship flips between the thigh and popliteal fossa. Forgetting this leads to compression errors and missed DVT.","tip":"In the popliteal fossa: <b>vein is superficial</b> (anterior) to the artery. This is the opposite of the thigh arrangement. Remember \"VAIN\" — Vein is Anterior In the popliteal fossa. Compression should collapse the vein without compressing the artery."}